{"ts":"2026-07-27T04:05:01.742Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"3bf0551381f1aa9315eb27c0","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-44u3wt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Daily auto-release never runs in its declared window: all 84 scheduled runs fired 2.5-4 hours after the cron time, so the release clock is undocumented drift"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Measured 2026-07-27 against the live workflow history. auto-release.yml declares schedule cron \"35 2 * * *\" and has declared exactly that value in every commit that touched the file since 2026-06-24. The GitHub API reports 84 runs for event=schedule. Not one of them started inside the declared window. The twenty most recent scheduled starts range from 05:10:04Z to 06:29:57Z, clustering near 05:35Z, which is a systematic lag of roughly three hours rather than the few minutes of jitter the platform documents. The declared cron is therefore not a description of when the project releases; it is a value nothing has ever validated against observed behaviour. Two consequences follow. First, the same-day guard computes its date key at run time, not at scheduled time, so the boundary that enforces one automatic release per day is anchored to a drifting instant that no configuration states. Second, any operator reading the workflow file forms a false expectation of the release window, and the release-health reminder that asks whether the daily release happened has no declared instant to compare against."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:release","ci","observability","reliability","scheduling"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-27T04:05:01.742Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-27T04:05:01.742Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The observed scheduled start time is measured against the declared cron and the divergence is reported rather than assumed to be jitter; The release window is expressed as a policy the project can assert, so a run that starts outside it is a detectable condition rather than an invisible one; The same-day release guard keys off an instant whose definition is stated in the workflow and does not silently move with platform scheduling lag; The release-health verification procedure names the window it expects, so a missing release is distinguishable from a late one"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make the automatic release clock an asserted, observable contract instead of an unvalidated cron literal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Operators and agents can tell a late release from a failed one, and the one-release-per-day guarantee rests on a stated instant"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"The 2026-07-27 release was not produced by the schedule at all; it was driven by two manual dispatches, and the scheduled run for the day will find the work already done and skip, which reads as success"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"GitHub Actions hosted runners, unbraind/pm-cli, workflow auto-release.yml, measured via the workflow runs API filtered to event=schedule"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run: gh api \"repos/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/workflows/auto-release.yml/runs?event=schedule&per_page=100\" --jq \".workflow_runs[].created_at\" and compare every value against the cron literal in .github/workflows/auto-release.yml"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Scheduled auto-release runs start within a small, stated tolerance of the declared cron window, or the divergence is surfaced"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"All 84 scheduled runs started 2.5 to 4 hours late; the declared 02:35Z window has never once been observed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-7zs0","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-27T04:05:01.742Z"},{"id":"pm-k6t4yb","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-27T04:05:01.742Z"},{"id":"pm-u9d0","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-07-27T04:05:01.742Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"47be61495215412e942dc3829d81d8dd8b7fe8198780744b2ea1ce7ebdab85f2","message":"File the release-window skew found while verifying the daily auto-release"}
